  "notes": "Nonprofit foundation, modified cash basis; treated as a single governmental-type fund, total column (all net asset classes). Beginning/ending 'cash' are total net assets (2,367,542 and 2,821,288) because that is what the statement rolls forward; transfers among net asset classes net to zero. Detail = Statement of Functional Expenses (2025 columns) by function column; the temporary-restricted net assets schedule (p4) is a subset of the same receipts/disbursements and the cash schedule (p5) has no revenue/expense lines, so neither is recorded in detail (no double counting). Balance sheet is the Modified Cash Basis statement of assets, liabilities and net assets (2025 column). Read pages 1-5 of 5",
  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "The foundation's statement (p2) rolls forward total net assets, not cash: beginning net assets 2,367,542 vs. 2024 cash and cash equivalents 1,671,001 (p1), ending net assets 2,821,288 vs. 2025 cash and cash equivalents 1,769,049 (p1; the rest is certificate of deposit 149,127, investments 605,179, board-designated endowment 313,008, less payroll tax payable 15,075). Should beginning_cash/ending_cash hold the printed cash and cash equivalents instead of total net assets (the roll-forward would then not tie, e.g. because of the 47,370 unrealized gain)?",
      "amount": 2821288,
      "recorded_as": "beginning_cash 2,367,542 and ending_cash 2,821,288 = total net assets (p2), so beginning + receipts - disbursements = ending ties; cash lines are in balance_sheet assets",
      "source_page": 2
    }
  ]
}
